@* Wraps a converted page in the master page it chose at RUNTIME.

   WebForms let a page pick its master in OnPreInit, and real applications use it: BlogEngine
   reads the theme from settings and assigns
   "~/Custom/Themes/{theme}/site.master" on every request. Blazor's @layout is decided when
   the component is compiled, so a page whose master is a string computed at run time cannot
   express it that way.

   LayoutView can - it takes the layout as a value. The page decides, then wraps its own
   content, which is the same shape WebForms had: the content page names the master and the
   master renders around it.

   When nothing resolves - a page that never assigns MasterPageFile, or one naming a master
   that was not converted - the content renders on its own. That is what the page did before
   this component existed, so a page this cannot help is left exactly as it was rather than
   wrapped in a layout picked to have something to show.
*@
@namespace WebForm2Blazor.Components

@if (Layout is null)
{
    @ChildContent
}
else
{
    <LayoutView Layout="@Layout">@ChildContent</LayoutView>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The page whose MasterPageFile decides the layout.</summary>
    [Parameter] public Page Owner { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public RenderFragment ChildContent { get; set; }

    private Type Layout => MasterPageCatalog.Resolve(Owner?.MasterPageFile);
}
